iteration): three DGROUP near-offset base-losses -> SIGSEGV in FUN_0000_02c5 (`*param_2=0` on a raw offset).

ROOT CAUSE (asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin @ image 0x4691..0x46dd; OBSERVED reached on the
genuine BATTLES(160,100)->OK(205,128)->ACCEPT(40,186) AZER1 run once patch 295's cooperative pump makes
[0x452] advance -- the block gates on `[0x452]-[0x6d1a] >= 0x1e0` (~480 ticks), NEVER true while [0x452]
was frozen; gdb core bt = 459a->4691->02c5, SIGSEGV at fist.c:4553 `*param_2=0`, param_2=0x6d0a).  4691:

    4691: mov ax,[0x452]; sub ax,[0x6d1a]; cmp ax,0x1e0; jb 0x46dd   ; every ~480 ticks
    469d: mov [0x6d1a],[0x452]; mov ax,[0x6d14]; movw [0x6d14],0; push ax
    46ad: shr ax,1 x3                            ; ax = uVar1>>3
    46b3: mov si,0x6d0a; call 0x2c5              ; 02c5(ax, si=0x6d0a DGROUP off) -> movb [si],0
    46b9: movb [0x6d0f],0x2e; pop bx; and bx,7; shl bx,1
    46c4: mov ax,[bx+0x6d1c]; mov [0x6d10],ax    ; read DGROUP:(bx+0x6d1c)
    46cb: movb [0x6d12],0
    46d0: mov si,0x6d0c; mov bx,0xa; mov cx,5; call [0x298]   ; (*c298)(si=0x6d0c,bx=0xa,cx=5)

Three near-offset (DS=DGROUP=0x1c00) values were dereferenced as HOST addresses:
  1. FUN_0000_02c5(uVar1>>3, 0x6d0a): 02c5's `movb [si],0` writes DGROUP:si; its contract (every OTHER
     caller -- 13876/19298/21319/21554/21654) passes a HOST pointer `&DAT_1000_df8c`, but 4691 passed the
     raw offset 0x6d0a -> *param_2=0 wrote host 0x6d0a -> SIGSEGV.  Pass g_mem+0x1c000+0x6d0a.
  2. `*(undefined2 *)((uVar1&7)*2 + 0x6d1c)` (46c4 `mov ax,[bx+0x6d1c]`): host read of ~0x6d1c -> SIGSEGV.
     Rebase onto g_mem+0x1c000+(uint16)((uVar1&7)*2+0x6d1c).
  3. (*c298)() dropped si=0x6d0c/bx=0xa/cx=5 (46d0..46d9).  c298's __allregs order = (di,bx,cx,si) per the
     threaded site fist.c:28553 (b152: di preserved, si set, bx=0xc, cx=0xa -> `(di,0xc,0xa,si)`).  4691
     does not set di, so pass 0 (a defined value; the other no-arg c298 sites 27419/30796 tolerate it and
     it is the periodic status-panel setup whose destination is si=0x6d0c, not di).

FIX: rebase the two host-ptr derefs onto g_mem+0x1c000 and thread the c298 register args.  All faithful to
the asm; no control-flow change.

